WEBVTT

00:00.210 --> 00:02.295
- We're told that cars A, B, and C

00:02.295 --> 00:04.629
are traveling at constant speeds

00:04.629 --> 00:08.241
and they say select the car
that travels the fastest

00:08.241 --> 00:10.573
and we have these three scenarios here.

00:10.573 --> 00:12.443
So, I encourage you to pause this video

00:12.443 --> 00:14.984
and try to figure out
which of these three cars

00:14.984 --> 00:16.734
is traveling the fastest,

00:16.734 --> 00:18.651
car A, car B, or car C.

00:19.442 --> 00:21.333
Alright, let's work through
this together.

00:21.333 --> 00:22.333
So, car A,

00:22.333 --> 00:24.678
they clearly just give its speed,

00:24.678 --> 00:27.111
it's 50 kilometers per hour.

00:27.111 --> 00:27.944
Now, let's see,

00:27.944 --> 00:30.261
car B travels the distance of D kilometers

00:30.261 --> 00:31.094
in H hours

00:32.071 --> 00:34.688
based on the equation 55h

00:34.688 --> 00:37.402
is equal to D.

00:37.402 --> 00:40.078
Alright, now, let's see if
we can translate this somehow

00:40.078 --> 00:42.256
into kilometers per hour.

00:42.256 --> 00:44.060
So, 55h is equal to D

00:44.060 --> 00:45.663
or we could say D

00:45.663 --> 00:48.795
is equal to 55H

00:48.795 --> 00:50.542
and here I'm doing,

00:50.542 --> 00:51.968
this is this scenario right over here,

00:51.968 --> 00:53.445
not scenario A.

00:53.445 --> 00:54.929
And so, another way
to think about it is

00:54.929 --> 00:56.708
distance divided by time,

00:56.708 --> 00:58.664
so if we divide both sides by hours,

00:58.664 --> 01:01.527
we would have distance divided by time,

01:01.527 --> 01:03.777
and so if we have D over H,

01:04.812 --> 01:07.654
then we would just be left
with 55 on the right hand side.

01:07.654 --> 01:09.483
All I did is I divided both sides

01:09.483 --> 01:11.278
by H.

01:11.278 --> 01:13.986
Now, this is distance divided by time,

01:13.986 --> 01:15.861
so the units here are going to be,

01:15.861 --> 01:16.694
we're assuming,

01:16.694 --> 01:17.934
and it tells us D is in kilometers,

01:17.934 --> 01:19.185
H is in hours,

01:19.185 --> 01:20.861
so the units here are going to be

01:20.861 --> 01:22.528
kilometers per hour.

01:23.609 --> 01:26.634
So, car B is going 55 kilometers per hour

01:26.634 --> 01:30.057
while car A is only going
50 kilometers per hour.

01:30.057 --> 01:32.882
So, so far, car B is the fastest.

01:32.882 --> 01:36.965
Now, car C travels 135
kilometers in three hours.

01:38.671 --> 01:40.454
Well, let's just get the hourly rate

01:40.454 --> 01:42.376
or I guess you could say the unit rate.

01:42.376 --> 01:45.293
So, 135 kilometers

01:47.409 --> 01:50.409
in three hours,

01:50.409 --> 01:52.787
and so we can get the rate per hour,

01:52.787 --> 01:55.998
so 135 divided by three is what?

01:55.998 --> 01:57.481
That is going to be,

01:57.481 --> 01:58.734
let's do it in our head,

01:58.734 --> 01:59.644
I think it's 45

01:59.644 --> 02:00.806
but let me just verify that,

02:00.806 --> 02:03.022
three goes into 135,

02:03.022 --> 02:04.729
three goes into 13 four times,

02:04.729 --> 02:06.673
four times three is 12.

02:06.673 --> 02:08.205
You subtract,

02:08.205 --> 02:09.367
you get, yep,

02:09.367 --> 02:11.781
three goes into 15 five times,

02:11.781 --> 02:13.737
five times three is 15.

02:13.737 --> 02:14.981
Subtract zero.

02:14.981 --> 02:17.270
So, this is equal to 45

02:17.270 --> 02:18.937
kilometers per hour.

02:20.108 --> 02:21.894
So, car A is 50 kilometers per hour,

02:21.894 --> 02:24.186
car B is 55 kilometers per hour,

02:24.186 --> 02:26.480
car C is 45 kilometers per hour,

02:26.480 --> 02:29.190
so car B is the fastest.
